@lang pt
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cp-dominio`
IMPORT `cp-pena`

-- Código Penal, Parte Geral, Título V — os SUBSTANTIVOS da aplicação da pena.
-- Written by g1b. DECLARE only: no rule, no constant, no directive. Every
-- other g1b module imports it.
--
-- What the Título V articles read that `cp-dominio` does not have:
--   * the agent's PRIOR CONVICTIONS, from which arts. 63 and 64 decide
--     reincidência (g0's `Agente`'s `reincidente` is the certified status;
--     `cp-g1b-circunstancias.l4` computes it, and its tests check the two
--     agree);
--   * the crime being sentenced, with the classifications the Parte Geral
--     turns on (culposo, a crime against the public administration, a crime
--     against sexual dignity, ...) — each a classification the offence's own
--     article or the court supplies (delegated-to-fact forks, notes/g1b.md);
--   * the findings arts. 61, 62, 65 and 66 read where the Code's words are
--     judgements ("motivo fútil", "relevante valor social ou moral") or facts
--     `cp-dominio` does not carry ("embriaguez preordenada");
--   * the judge's own determinations: the valuation of art. 59's
--     circumstances, the quantities fixed in each phase, the species chosen.
--     The encoding never makes these; it checks them against the Code.

§ `Título V — Das penas: os fatos da condenação (g1b)`

§§ `A espécie aplicada`

-- PROPOSTO-COMUM: g1c's arts. 77 and 83 read the penalty the sentence applied
-- and its species; so does any encoder of a sentence.
-- The species the SENTENCE applies. `cp-pena`'s `Espécie de pena privativa de
-- liberdade` has a third member, `reclusão ou detenção`, for the preceitos
-- that leave the choice to the judge (arts. 235 § 1º, 306 parágrafo único).
-- Once the judge has chosen (art. 59, I), only two remain; a separate type
-- makes an undecided species unwritable in an applied penalty.
DECLARE `Espécie aplicada` IS ONE OF
    `pena de reclusão`
    @nlg:en a penalty of reclusão
    `pena de detenção`
    @nlg:en a penalty of detenção

§§ `A condenação anterior (arts. 63 e 64)`

-- PROPOSTO-COMUM: g1c needs prior convictions and reincidência too (arts. 77,
-- I and 81, I "reincidente em crime doloso"; art. 83; art. 110, caput; art.
-- 117, VI), and may not import this module. Hoist `Natureza da infração
-- anterior` and `Condenação anterior` to cp-dominio, with `Agente` carrying a
-- list of them; arts. 63–64's rules (`cp-g1b-circunstancias.l4`) then serve
-- both.
-- What the earlier offence was, in the words art. 63 and art. 64, II use.
-- "crime anterior" (art. 63) excludes a contravenção penal; art. 64, II takes
-- out "os crimes militares próprios e políticos".
DECLARE `Natureza da infração anterior` IS ONE OF
    `crime nem militar próprio nem político`
    @nlg:en a crime that is neither a purely military crime nor a political crime
    `crime militar próprio`
    @nlg:en a purely military crime
    `crime político`
    @nlg:en a political crime
    `contravenção penal`
    @nlg:en a misdemeanour (contravenção penal)

-- One final conviction, as the criminal record certifies it (Súmula 636 STJ,
-- M-sweep-a-13: the folha de antecedentes suffices; how it is proved is not
-- the encoding's). `identificação do processo` is identity: two records with
-- the same one are the same conviction (phrasebook entry 6.6).
DECLARE `Condenação anterior` HAS
    `identificação do processo` IS A STRING
    @nlg:en the identification of the case in which the agent was convicted
    `tipo penal` IS A STRING
    @nlg:en the offence of the conviction, as its article (e.g. "CP art. 155")
    `natureza da infração` IS A `Natureza da infração anterior`
    @nlg:en what kind of offence the conviction was for
    `crime doloso` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the earlier crime was intentional (doloso)
    `proferida no estrangeiro` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the conviction was handed down abroad
    `data do trânsito em julgado` IS A DATE
    @nlg:en the day the conviction became final (trânsito em julgado)
    `data do cumprimento ou da extinção da pena` IS A MAYBE DATE
    @nlg:en the day the penalty was served or extinguished, if it has been
    `início do período de prova da suspensão ou do livramento condicional, sem revogação` IS A MAYBE DATE
    @nlg:en the day a probation period (suspended sentence or parole) began, where there was one and it was not revoked

§§ `O crime em julgamento`

-- Classifications of the crime being sentenced that a Parte Geral article
-- turns on. None is a fact a witness gives: each is the offence's own (its
-- Título, its culposo form) or the court's (whether it "envolver violência
-- sexual contra a mulher"). They are supplied, and each is a
-- delegated-to-fact fork in notes/g1b.md. A member present means it holds.
DECLARE `Classificação do crime` IS ONE OF
    `crime contra a administração pública`
    @nlg:en a crime against the public administration (Título XI of the Parte Especial)
    `crime contra a dignidade sexual`
    @nlg:en a crime against sexual dignity (Título VI of the Parte Especial)
    `crime culposo de trânsito`
    @nlg:en a negligent traffic crime
    `crime que envolve violência sexual contra a mulher`
    @nlg:en a crime involving sexual violence against a woman
    `crime cometido no exercício de profissão, atividade, ofício, cargo ou função, com violação dos deveres que lhes são inerentes`
    @nlg:en a crime committed in the exercise of a profession, activity, trade, office or function, in breach of its duties

-- The findings and facts arts. 61, 62, 65 and 66 read that are not in
-- `cp-dominio`. The Code's own words; a member present means the court found
-- it. Where the Code's words are a judgement ("fútil", "relevante valor") the
-- member records the judge's finding, and the encoding never computes it.
DECLARE `Achado das circunstâncias legais` IS ONE OF
    -- art. 61, II, a
    `motivo fútil`
    @nlg:en a futile motive
    `motivo torpe`
    @nlg:en a base (torpe) motive
    -- art. 61, II, b
    `para facilitar ou assegurar a execução, a ocultação, a impunidade ou vantagem de outro crime`
    @nlg:en to facilitate or secure the execution, concealment, impunity or advantage of another crime
    -- art. 61, II, c (traição, emboscada and dissimulação are `Meio empregado`s)
    `outro recurso que dificultou ou tornou impossível a defesa do ofendido`
    @nlg:en another device that made the victim's defence difficult or impossible
    -- art. 61, II, d (veneno, fogo and tortura are `Meio empregado`s)
    `emprego de explosivo`
    @nlg:en the use of an explosive
    `outro meio insidioso ou cruel`
    @nlg:en another insidious or cruel means
    `meio de que podia resultar perigo comum`
    @nlg:en a means that could cause common danger
    -- art. 61, II, f
    `abuso de autoridade`
    @nlg:en abuse of authority
    `o agente prevaleceu-se de relações domésticas, de coabitação ou de hospitalidade`
    @nlg:en the agent took advantage of domestic relations, cohabitation or hospitality
    `violência contra a mulher na forma da lei específica`
    @nlg:en violence against a woman as the specific law (Lei Maria da Penha) defines it
    -- art. 61, II, g
    `abuso de poder ou violação de dever inerente a cargo, ofício, ministério ou profissão`
    @nlg:en abuse of power or breach of a duty inherent in an office, trade, ministry or profession
    -- art. 61, II, i
    `o ofendido estava sob a imediata proteção da autoridade`
    @nlg:en the victim was under the immediate protection of the authorities
    -- art. 61, II, j (the calamities are a `Circunstância do fato`)
    `em ocasião de desgraça particular do ofendido`
    @nlg:en at a time of the victim's personal misfortune
    -- art. 61, II, l
    `em estado de embriaguez preordenada`
    @nlg:en in a state of premeditated drunkenness
    -- art. 62 (IV reads the `Meio empregado` `paga ou promessa de recompensa`)
    `promoveu ou organizou a cooperação no crime ou dirigiu a atividade dos demais agentes`
    @nlg:en promoted or organised the cooperation in the crime, or directed the other agents
    `coagiu ou induziu outrem à execução material do crime`
    @nlg:en coerced or induced another to carry out the crime
    `instigou ou determinou a cometer o crime alguém sujeito à sua autoridade ou não-punível em virtude de condição ou qualidade pessoal`
    @nlg:en instigated or caused someone under their authority, or not punishable because of a personal condition, to commit the crime
    -- art. 65, II
    `desconhecimento da lei`
    @nlg:en ignorance of the law
    -- art. 65, III, a
    `motivo de relevante valor social ou moral`
    @nlg:en a motive of relevant social or moral value
    -- art. 65, III, b
    `procurou, por sua espontânea vontade e com eficiência, logo após o crime, evitar-lhe ou minorar-lhe as consequências`
    @nlg:en of their own free will and effectively, soon after the crime, tried to avoid or lessen its consequences
    `reparou o dano antes do julgamento`
    @nlg:en repaired the damage before judgment
    -- art. 65, III, c
    `sob coação a que podia resistir`
    @nlg:en under coercion the agent could have resisted
    `em cumprimento de ordem de autoridade superior`
    @nlg:en in compliance with an order of a superior authority
    `sob a influência de violenta emoção, provocada por ato injusto da vítima`
    @nlg:en under the influence of violent emotion provoked by an unjust act of the victim
    -- art. 65, III, d (fork F-sweep-a-11)
    `confessou espontaneamente, perante a autoridade, a autoria do crime`
    @nlg:en spontaneously confessed, before the authorities, to being the author of the crime
    `confessou em parte ou de forma qualificada`
    @nlg:en confessed in part or with a qualification, admitting less than the crime charged
    -- art. 65, III, e
    `sob a influência de multidão em tumulto`
    @nlg:en under the influence of a rioting crowd
    `provocou o tumulto`
    @nlg:en the agent provoked the riot
    -- art. 66
    `circunstância relevante, anterior ou posterior ao crime, não prevista expressamente em lei`
    @nlg:en a relevant circumstance, before or after the crime, not expressly provided by law

-- The circumstances of arts. 61 and 62 as the RESULT the second phase reads:
-- one member per inciso or alínea. Also the vocabulary of art. 61's caput
-- "quando não constituem ou qualificam o crime": the crime record lists those
-- that are elements or qualificadoras of the crime being sentenced.
DECLARE `Circunstância agravante` IS ONE OF
    `a reincidência (art. 61, I)`
    @nlg:en recidivism
    `motivo fútil ou torpe (art. 61, II, a)`
    @nlg:en a futile or base motive
    `para facilitar ou assegurar outro crime (art. 61, II, b)`
    @nlg:en to facilitate or secure another crime
    `à traição, de emboscada, mediante dissimulação ou outro recurso (art. 61, II, c)`
    @nlg:en by treachery, ambush, dissimulation or another device hindering defence
    `com veneno, fogo, explosivo, tortura ou outro meio insidioso, cruel ou de perigo comum (art. 61, II, d)`
    @nlg:en with poison, fire, explosive, torture or another insidious, cruel or commonly dangerous means
    `contra ascendente, descendente, irmão ou cônjuge (art. 61, II, e)`
    @nlg:en against an ascendant, descendant, sibling or spouse
    `com abuso de autoridade, relações domésticas ou violência contra a mulher (art. 61, II, f)`
    @nlg:en with abuse of authority, domestic relations, or violence against a woman
    `com abuso de poder ou violação de dever (art. 61, II, g)`
    @nlg:en with abuse of power or breach of duty
    `contra criança, maior de 60 anos, enfermo ou mulher grávida (art. 61, II, h)`
    @nlg:en against a child, a person over sixty, an ill person or a pregnant woman
    `quando o ofendido estava sob a imediata proteção da autoridade (art. 61, II, i)`
    @nlg:en when the victim was under the immediate protection of the authorities
    `em ocasião de calamidade pública ou de desgraça particular do ofendido (art. 61, II, j)`
    @nlg:en during a public calamity or the victim's personal misfortune
    `em estado de embriaguez preordenada (art. 61, II, l)`
    @nlg:en in premeditated drunkenness
    `nas dependências de instituição de ensino (art. 61, II, m)`
    @nlg:en on the premises of an educational institution
    `promove, organiza ou dirige (art. 62, I)`
    @nlg:en the agent promoted, organised or directed the crime
    `coage ou induz outrem à execução (art. 62, II)`
    @nlg:en the agent coerced or induced another to carry it out
    `instiga ou determina subordinado ou não-punível (art. 62, III)`
    @nlg:en the agent instigated a subordinate or a non-punishable person
    `mediante paga ou promessa de recompensa (art. 62, IV)`
    @nlg:en the agent acted for payment or the promise of a reward

-- The circumstances of arts. 65 and 66, likewise. The confession is two
-- members because the STJ's revised Súmulas 545 and 630 (fork
-- F-sweep-a-11) make a partial or qualified confession attenuate "em
-- proporção inferior": the difference is the judge's to weigh, and the
-- encoding keeps the two apart so the judge can.
DECLARE `Circunstância atenuante` IS ONE OF
    `a idade do agente (art. 65, I)`
    @nlg:en the agent's age (under 21 at the act, or over 70 at the sentence)
    `o desconhecimento da lei (art. 65, II)`
    @nlg:en ignorance of the law
    `o relevante valor social ou moral (art. 65, III, a)`
    @nlg:en a motive of relevant social or moral value
    `a minoração das consequências ou a reparação do dano (art. 65, III, b)`
    @nlg:en lessening the consequences, or repairing the damage before judgment
    `a coação resistível, a ordem superior ou a violenta emoção (art. 65, III, c)`
    @nlg:en resistible coercion, a superior order, or violent emotion provoked by the victim
    `a confissão espontânea (art. 65, III, d)`
    @nlg:en a spontaneous confession
    `a confissão parcial ou qualificada (art. 65, III, d)`
    @nlg:en a partial or qualified confession
    `a influência de multidão em tumulto (art. 65, III, e)`
    @nlg:en the influence of a rioting crowd the agent did not provoke
    `a circunstância relevante do art. 66`
    @nlg:en a relevant circumstance not expressly provided by law

-- The crime being sentenced: the shared `Agente`, `Vítima` and `Fato`, plus
-- what the Parte Geral reads.
DECLARE `Crime em julgamento` HAS
    agente IS AN Agente
    @nlg:en the agent being sentenced
    `vítima` IS A MAYBE `Vítima`
    @nlg:en the victim, where the victim is a natural person
    fato IS A Fato
    @nlg:en the act
    `tipo penal` IS A STRING
    @nlg:en the offence being sentenced, as its article (e.g. "CP art. 155")
    `pena cominada` IS A `Pena cominada`
    @nlg:en the penalty the offence's article prescribes, in the form that applies to the case
    culposo IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the crime is negligent (culposo), not intentional
    `classificações` IS A LIST OF `Classificação do crime`
    @nlg:en the classifications of the crime that the Parte Geral reads
    `condenações anteriores` IS A LIST OF `Condenação anterior`
    @nlg:en the agent's earlier final convictions
    `inquéritos ou ações penais em curso` IS A NUMBER
    @nlg:en how many police inquiries or prosecutions against the agent are pending
    `achados` IS A LIST OF `Achado das circunstâncias legais`
    @nlg:en the facts and findings the court made on the circumstances of arts. 61, 62, 65 and 66
    `agravantes que constituem ou qualificam o crime` IS A LIST OF `Circunstância agravante`
    @nlg:en the aggravating circumstances that are already elements or qualifying circumstances of this crime

§§ `As determinações do juiz (art. 59)`

-- How the judge valued each circumstance of art. 59. The valuation is the
-- judge's; `neutra` is a circumstance the judge did not weigh either way.
DECLARE `Valoração` IS ONE OF
    `favorável`
    @nlg:en favourable to the accused
    neutra
    @nlg:en neither favourable nor unfavourable
    `desfavorável`
    @nlg:en unfavourable to the accused

DECLARE `Circunstâncias judiciais` HAS
    culpabilidade IS A `Valoração`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the culpability
    antecedentes IS A `Valoração`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the record (antecedentes)
    `conduta social` IS A `Valoração`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the social conduct
    personalidade IS A `Valoração`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the personality of the agent
    motivos IS A `Valoração`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the motives
    `circunstâncias do crime` IS A `Valoração`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the circumstances of the crime
    `consequências do crime` IS A `Valoração`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the consequences of the crime
    `comportamento da vítima` IS A `Valoração`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the behaviour of the victim
    -- What the valuation of the antecedentes and of the victim's behaviour
    -- rested on; the tests of forks F-sweep-a-02 and F-sweep-a-03 and of
    -- M-sweep-a-04 (ADPF 1.107) read these.
    `condenações valoradas como antecedentes` IS A LIST OF STRING
    @nlg:en the case identifications of the convictions weighed as a bad record
    `inquéritos ou ações penais em curso valorados como antecedentes` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en pending inquiries or prosecutions were weighed as a bad record
    `comportamento da vítima valorado pela vida sexual pregressa ou pelo modo de vida da vítima` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the victim's behaviour was weighed on the victim's prior sexual life or way of life

-- The sentence as the judge wrote it: the circumstances, the quantity each
-- phase of art. 68 reached, the species chosen, and the judgements arts. 33
-- § 3º and 44 leave to the judge.
DECLARE `Sentença` HAS
    crime IS A `Crime em julgamento`
    @nlg:en the crime being sentenced
    `data da sentença` IS A DATE
    @nlg:en the day of the sentence
    `circunstâncias judiciais` IS A `Circunstâncias judiciais`
    @nlg:en how the judge valued the circumstances of art. 59
    `pena-base` IS A Duração
    @nlg:en the base penalty the judge fixed in the first phase
    `pena provisória` IS A Duração
    @nlg:en the provisional penalty the judge fixed in the second phase
    `pena aplicada` IS A Duração
    @nlg:en the final custodial penalty the judge fixed
    `espécie aplicada` IS AN `Espécie aplicada`
    @nlg:en the kind of custodial penalty applied
    `a substituição é suficiente, a juízo do juiz` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the judge found that substituting the custodial penalty is sufficient (art. 44, III)
    `a substituição é socialmente recomendável, em face da condenação anterior` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the judge found substitution socially advisable despite the earlier conviction (art. 44, § 3º)
    `fundamentação concreta e idônea para regime mais gravoso` IS A BOOLEAN
    @nlg:en the judge gave a concrete, proper reason, other than the crime's abstract gravity, for a harsher initial regime

§§ `A pena aplicada a cada crime, no concurso (arts. 69 a 76)`

-- One crime's penalty as the judge fixed it, for the rules of concurso.
DECLARE `Pena aplicada a um crime` HAS
    `identificação do crime` IS A STRING
    @nlg:en which crime this penalty is for
    `espécie` IS AN `Espécie aplicada`
    @nlg:en the kind of custodial penalty applied for this crime
    quantidade IS A Duração
    @nlg:en the custodial penalty fixed for this crime
    `data do fato` IS A DATE
    @nlg:en the day of this crime
    `multa aplicada` IS A MAYBE `Multa aplicada`
    @nlg:en the fine imposed for this crime, if any
